---
import Site from '../layouts/Site.astro';
import '../styles/get-help.css';
import Hero from '../components/Hero.astro';
import Support from '../components/Support.astro';
import { asset } from '../data/site';
---

<Site title="Dask | Get Help">
  <Hero title="Get Help" />
  <section class="help-content light-grid">
    <div class="help-intro">
      <h2>Asking for help</h2>
      <p>
        We welcome usage questions and bug reports from all users, even those
        who are new to using the project. There are a few things you can do to
        improve the likelihood of quickly getting a good answer.
      </p>
      <div class="help-icons">
        <a href="https://github.com/dask/dask" aria-label="Ask on GitHub">
          <img src={asset('git-hub.svg')} alt="" />
        </a>
        <a href="https://dask.discourse.group" aria-label="Ask on Discourse">
          <img src={asset('chat.svg')} alt="" />
        </a>
      </div>
    </div>
    <div class="help-answers">
      <article>
        <h3>Ask questions in the right place</h3>
        <p>
          We strongly prefer the use of{' '}
          <a href="https://dask.discourse.group">Discourse</a> or{' '}
          <a href="https://github.com/dask/dask">GitHub</a>. Discourse and
          GitHub are more easily searchable by future users, and therefore can
          be useful to many more people than those directly involved. If you
          have a general question about how something should work or want best
          practices then use{' '}
          <a href="https://dask.discourse.group">Discourse</a>. If you think you
          have found a bug then use{' '}
          <a href="https://github.com/dask/dask">GitHub</a>
        </p>
      </article>
      <article>
        <h3>Ask only in one place</h3>
        <p>
          Please restrict yourself to posting your question in only one place
          (likely the Dask Discourse or GitHub) and don’t post in both
        </p>
      </article>
      <article>
        <h3>Create a minimal example</h3>
        <p>
          It is ideal to create minimal, complete, verifiable examples. This
          significantly reduces the time that answerers spend understanding your
          situation, resulting in higher quality answers more quickly.{' '}
          <a href="#">See also</a> this blog post about crafting minimal bug
          reports. These have a much higher likelihood of being answered
        </p>
      </article>
    </div>
  </section>
  <Support />
</Site>
